          A basement floor is the hardest place in the house to keep paint attached, and the reason is underneath it. The slab rests on soil that is rarely fully dry, and water vapor moves up through the concrete all year. Paint that would last a decade in a garage can blister in a basement within one humid summer. The good news is that the problem is predictable. Test the slab, deal with what the test shows, choose a paint built for below-grade concrete, and a painted basement floor is a durable, cheap upgrade.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />


        <!-- Picks -->
